 "notes_text": "An old-European musette waltz heard from the next room. KEPT: C minor 3/4 at 152, inverted um-pa-pa, a strict one-bar pendulum, a narrow line, a cry at bar 8, an early held tonic. CHANGED: the pendulum is plagal, i <-> iv (Cm <-> Fm), with the bass leaping C-F. It is just as hypnotic, but it is not the original's dominant rocking. HOOK: a limping musette lilt, dotted quarter + eighth + quarter, with chromatic lower neighbours: 'fa. mi-natural le | sol. fi mi'. E-natural and F# are the classic musette appoggiaturas. F#->Eb is an augmented second, and the up-a-fourth (E->Ab) / down-a-third answer gives the cell a shape you can hum ('daa-di DAA | daa-di da'). It is stated twice (bars 1-3). B section: the lilt climbs a step at a time (G, Ab, Bb with an A-natural neighbour), and a rising triplet run G-Ab-Bb plus B leads into the cry C6 at bar 8. C6 is a fourth suspended over V7 and resolves a semitone to B5 on the half-beat, then falls through a triplet Ab-G-F. The cadence restates the lilt (Ab. G), and the leading tone resolves an eighth early to C6, held. A second reed plays the melody in parallel thirds in bars 5-9 (the musette duo), which gives the B section its lift. Under the held tonic, iv returns as a plagal ghost that resolves into the loop. Revision d (melody judge's fixes, YARGI.md): bar 7's last beat is now vii°7 (B-D-F-Ab over the F bass) under the leading tone B5, so the triplet run lands on the diminished seventh and moves to the cry over V7 by common tones; in the B-section sequence (bars 5-6) the lilt's long note is re-struck on beat 2 (Ab | Ab-G | F, Bb | Bb-A | G), melody and second reed together, so the waltz's bright 'a' on 2 is in the melody through the build-up. The hook statement in bars 1-3, the cry and the cadence are unchanged.",
 "revision": {
  "of": "b2-2",
  "by": "melody-judge fix pass (DUZELTME.md)",
  "changes": [
   "bar 7 beat 3: iv (Fm) -> vii°7 (B-D-F-Ab), bass F kept; B5 is now a chord tone instead of sitting over iv",
   "bars 5-6: melody Ab5:1.5 G5:.5 F5:1 | Bb5:1.5 A5:.5 G5:1 -> Ab5:1 Ab5:.5 G5:.5 F5:1 | Bb5:1 Bb5:.5 A5:.5 G5:1 (the long note re-struck on beat 2); the counter's parallel thirds get the same rhythm",
   "everything else (hook bars 1-3, the i <-> iv pendulum, the triplet run, the C6 cry, the cadence, the hold) unchanged"
  ]
 }
